---
import Layout from '../../studio/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { mailto, studio } from '../../apps/registry';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Pausebell';
const description = 'Privacy policy for Pausebell (com.yanerapps.pausebell), a meditation course and timer for Android by Yaner Apps.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <nav aria-label="Pausebell navigation" class="product-nav">
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy by app</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Pausebell
    </nav>
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Pausebell for Android (<code>com.yanerapps.pausebell</code>)</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Effective: from Pausebell&rsquo;s release on Google Play</span>
        <span>&middot;</span>
        <span>Updated: 16 Nov 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      This policy explains what Pausebell does with your data. Pausebell is made by Yaner Apps, an independent
      developer studio ("we", "us"). It applies to the Pausebell Android application and to this website.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
      <p><strong>In short:</strong> Pausebell has no user accounts, no servers of our own, and no permission to use
      the internet. Your sessions, notes and presets stay on your device. There are no ads and no analytics. If you
      buy Pro, Google Play handles the purchase and payment, and we never see your payment details. We never sell
      your personal information.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Data that stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The following is stored in the app's private storage and is never sent to us &mdash; we operate no server
      and have no way to read it:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your history: each saved session's start time, length, source (a lesson, a preset or the timer), whether it was completed, and your optional note</li>
      <li>Your presets and timer settings</li>
      <li>Course progress and settings, including the daily reminder's time and days</li>
      <li>Your Pro status, as a copy signed with a key that stays in your device's secure keystore</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can delete any session in History, delete presets, and reset course progress at any time.
      Uninstalling Pausebell removes everything stored on the device.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Permissions</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Permission</th>
            <th>What Pausebell does with it</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Notifications (optional)</td>
            <td>Shows the session in progress, with Pause and End, and the daily reminder if you turn it on</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Foreground service (media playback) and keeping the device awake</td>
            <td>Lets the bells ring on time while the screen is off during a session you started. It stops when the session ends</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Vibration</td>
            <td>Vibrates for bells you set to vibrate</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Run at startup</td>
            <td>Puts the daily reminder back after the device restarts. It never starts a session by itself</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Play billing</td>
            <td>Lets Google Play sell Pro and tell the app whether you have it</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Pausebell does not ask for your location, contacts, camera, microphone, calendar or files, and it has no
      internet permission of its own. The spoken cues in the course are recordings bundled with the app; the
      voice is computer-generated, and nothing you say or do is processed to make it.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Data sent to third parties</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Recipient</th>
            <th>What is sent</th>
            <th>Why</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Play (through the Play Store app)</td>
            <td>Your purchase of Pro, and requests to show the rating card</td>
            <td>To sell Pro and confirm that you have it, and to let you rate the app if you choose to</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Your history, notes, presets and settings are never sent to Google or to anyone else. Pausebell shows no
      ads and contains no advertising, analytics or crash-reporting SDK, so it does not use your advertising ID.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Buying Pro</h2>
    <p>
      Pausebell Pro is a one-time purchase sold and billed entirely by Google Play. Google Play takes the payment,
      and your payment method and billing details stay with Google. We never receive your card number, billing
      address or other payment information, and Pausebell has no server that receives your purchases. Google
      Play gives us order records for our sales in the Play Console, such as the order number, price and date,
      which we use only for accounting, refunds and support.
    </p>
    <p>
      To unlock Pro, the app asks Google Play whether you have it and keeps a signed copy of the answer in private
      storage, so Pro keeps working while you are offline. This copy is excluded from Android cloud backup and
      device-to-device transfer. If Pro is refunded, nothing in your history or presets is changed or deleted.
      Google's handling of payment data is governed by the
      <a href="https://payments.google.com/payments/apis-secure/u/0/get_legal_document?ldo=0&amp;ldt=privacynotice" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Payments Privacy Notice</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Exports and backups</h2>
    <p>
      Pausebell can export your history as a CSV file when you ask for it, and hands it to the app you pick in
      Android's share sheet. Once it leaves Pausebell, it is yours to protect.
    </p>
    <p>
      Android's own cloud backup may include your history, presets and settings if you have enabled it on your
      device; your Pro status, a session in progress and the timing of the rating card are left out. That backup
      is managed by Google under your Google account, not by us.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Notifications and the widget</h2>
    <p>
      The session notification, the Quick Settings tile and the home screen widget show a preset's name and the
      time left, so anyone who can see your screen can see them. You can hide notification content on the lock
      screen in Android's settings.
    </p>

    <h2>7. What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No user accounts, sign-in, or profiles</li>
      <li>No servers operated by us, and therefore no copy of your history held by us</li>
      <li>No ads, analytics or crash-reporting SDKs</li>
      <li>No internet permission in the app itself</li>
      <li>No location, microphone or health data</li>
      <li>No sale of personal information</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Pausebell is meant for adults and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from
      children; since the app sends us nothing, a child's history would stay on their device like anyone else's.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Because your data lives on your device, you control its lifetime: it stays until you delete it or uninstall
      the app. There is nothing for us to delete on our side, since we hold nothing. Data held by Google as a
      result of a purchase is subject to Google's own retention practices.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Your history is kept in the app's private storage, which other apps cannot read on a non-rooted device.
      Exported CSV files are not encrypted, so keep them somewhere safe.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Additional information for the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
    <p>
      This section gives the information required by the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation and
      the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection.
    </p>

    <h3>Controller</h3>
    <p>
      The controller for the processing described in this policy is Yaner Yang, publishing as Yaner Apps,
      reachable at <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a>. Google acts as an independent
      controller for the data it receives, under its own policies.
    </p>

    <h3>Purposes and legal bases</h3>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Data</th>
            <th>Legal basis</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Providing Pro you bought</td>
            <td>Your Google Play purchase status and the order records Google Play provides</td>
            <td>Necessary to perform the contract you entered into when buying Pro (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Answering your emails</td>
            <td>Your email address and your message</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests in responding to you (Art. 6(1)(f)); we delete the correspondence once the matter is closed, and within 12 months at the latest</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Data that stays on your device (section 1) is not processed by us at all. You are not required to
      provide any personal data. We make no decisions based solely on automated processing.
    </p>

    <h3>International transfers</h3>
    <p>
      Google may process purchase data in the United States and other countries, relying on the EU-U.S. Data
      Privacy Framework, its UK Extension and the Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, and on Standard
      Contractual Clauses where needed (see
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy/frameworks" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's data transfer frameworks</a>).
    </p>

    <h3>Your rights under the GDPR</h3>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, rectify and erase your personal data, to restrict or object to its
      processing, and to data portability. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
      protection supervisory authority, in particular in the country where you live or work; in the UK this
      is the Information Commissioner's Office, and in Switzerland the Federal Data Protection and
      Information Commissioner. Section 12 explains how to exercise these rights.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or port your personal data.
      Since Pausebell stores your data only on your device, you can exercise these rights directly in the app:
      delete sessions or presets, and export your history as CSV to take it elsewhere. If you need help, write to
      <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a> and we will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version is published on this page with a new "updated" date. A later
      version may offer optional writing of your sessions to Health Connect; this policy will describe it before
      that feature is released.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Yaner Apps &mdash; <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
